% Declarations: pairwise distinctness of the purposes.
%
% DPV publishes nothing that separates these purposes.  It defines
% each as a purpose in its own right, and a verdict resting on an
% instance of the declarations is withdrawable by abandoning them.
%
% Distinctness, not disjointness: one purpose may lie below another
% and still be a different purpose.  Disjointness over a pair with a
% common child would contradict the resource, and this module
% publishes concepts below two parents.
%
% The rule is stated here and instantiated by the problems.  A
% problem naming two of the purposes below carries the inequation
% between them as a bg_dist_ statement.
%
% Purposes: 121
% Pairs   : 7260
%
% AcademicResearch, AccountManagement, Advertising, AgeVerification, CombatClimateChange, CommercialPurpose, CommercialResearch, CommunicationForCustomerCare
% CommunicationManagement, CounterMoneyLaundering, Counterterrorism, CustomerCare, CustomerClaimsManagement, CustomerManagement, CustomerOrderManagement, CustomerRelationshipManagement
